<description>&lt;p&gt;Bomb attacks in Thailand's south injured two police officers, prompting tighter security and expanded border intelligence, while Cambodia is hosting ASEAN observers and raising the border dispute at international forums with US support pledged by Hun Manet, who thanked Trump. Myanmar’s military leader Min Aung Hlaing accused Thailand of aiding illegal border trade, and a $3 million project will train 4,500 Myanmar refugees for Thai jobs. Malaysia is funding a RM200 million rail link to the border, and Thailand is discussing aviation hub status and cross-border water pollution with China. The UCDP recorded 35 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxQM1ZYekN3akNwYmpEM0pTR3ZBOFAyZ3NlVEdOeW5Yal93WTdQNVhpU3dELUhRS1Nfa1RDa1V1aXhIbVZmZ05IcXl4OXhoLXRMTnNxQW9WUzF5bHFCaG1BR1B0OWF0dGZCWmhZcTE1T3EzbTNpbkJ6OUdZOGhlY2ZiR016YVNvMFVSVjB3dXVXQ0JxdXowNzhKUVRR?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Irrawaddy&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Star&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuwFBVV95cUxNSTF0V01FQ2pmYUdfQ3JleTk1TVZJNWFoYWRRRDZVVFRHb0dHWnFScmpYUGhDWVQ1ekE0QnZNWG1xY19nenh3bDYtb1JUR212ejlRSy16Ukl2Z29FNnU3UWNmUnF2V1ZMTVd2QUtjUTlOOWhyQWRoMHFrOGhfbV9haWZlM3lpRkluNDdIcmhQVTRLdEtmRXQ2Nnk5aVpPMzRaemsxZ3Jqck1YMWFrMTZGQXpRZmpzTGxhd0t3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Khmer Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiX0FVX3lxTE1Gand1eS1MTHVKZ1o3N3NqekpnMUtiN2JUOTNURVNFQnRvdXZwblFPb2RhOGxFQ0czTW5aN2JPb0JaNnIwWEtheWRTRkVGckZNNlM0Q0p1RzdaSTA1aUhN?oc=5&quot;&gt;Nation Thailand&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMib0FVX3lxTFAzbUNDanZGVTBqQTJPOGR1cW50VERrLXJfVzFVYmFONXBoVGZWNVp3VVZqMGdYbzJhSU1BaVlodGtqS1FWNUd5QlB6WlNBM1dJLXZYaHpTTnhYeTZLeEw4NWkwM05RQ